---
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import BaseHead from '../components/BaseHead.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
import Header from '../components/Header.astro';

import personImage from '../assets/about/person.png';
import potaImage from '../assets/about/pota.png';
import fieldImage from '../assets/about/field.png';
import deskImage from '../assets/about/desk.png';
import moonImage from '../assets/astrophotography/iss-over-the-moon/iss-across-the-moon.jpg';
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <BaseHead
      title="About — Chips’nCode"
      description="Who is behind Chips’nCode, and why biology, teaching, radio, code, astrophotography, fieldwork, and miniature painting have all ended up under one roof."
    />
  </head>
  <body>
    <Header />

    <main class="about-page">
      <section class="about-hero panel">
        <div class="about-hero__copy">
          <p class="about-kicker">About</p>
          <h1 class="about-title">A life stitched together from science, code, tinkering, poetry, paint and the cosmos.</h1>
          <p class="about-lede">
            I am a teacher, biologist, molecular biologist, ecologist, environmentalist, tinkerer, photographer, poet,
            radio tragic, space enthusiast, computer geek, and painter of 3D printed miniatures. I was also born at
            349.19 ppm of atmospheric CO₂, which matters to me because it places my life right on the edge of 350 ppm:
            one of those numbers that marks the point where we should have stopped and absolutely did not.
          </p>
          <p class="about-lede about-lede--small">
            Chips&rsquo;nCode is where all of that gets stacked into one place: code, fieldwork, lessons, radio, optics,
            ecology, astronomy, and whatever useful nonsense happens when we stop pretending they are separate.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="about-collage" aria-hidden="true">
          <figure class="about-shot about-shot--portrait">
            <Image src={personImage} alt="" widths={[520, 760]} sizes="(max-width: 900px) 80vw, 24vw" />
          </figure>
          <figure class="about-shot about-shot--radio">
            <Image src={potaImage} alt="" widths={[640, 960]} sizes="(max-width: 900px) 90vw, 32vw" />
          </figure>
          <figure class="about-shot about-shot--field">
            <Image src={fieldImage} alt="" widths={[640, 960]} sizes="(max-width: 900px) 86vw, 26vw" />
          </figure>
          <figure class="about-shot about-shot--moon">
            <Image src={moonImage} alt="" widths={[360, 560]} sizes="(max-width: 900px) 45vw, 14vw" />
          </figure>
          <div class="about-scribble about-scribble--one">cells ↔ circuits ↔ classrooms ↔ galaxies</div>
          <div class="about-scribble about-scribble--two">everything leaks into everything else</div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="about-spread">
        <aside class="about-margin panel panel--soft">
          <figure class="margin-photo">
            <Image src={deskImage} alt="A crowded workbench with radio gear, notes, painting tools, a snake, and chickens outside." widths={[720, 1080]} sizes="(max-width: 980px) 100vw, 28vw" />
          </figure>
          <p class="margin-note">
            The desk photo is not metaphorical. It really does look like that sometimes. Yes, there is a snake. Yes,
            there are chickens. No, I will not pretend my life arrives in neat thematic categories. Yes it is AI
            generated. No I will NOT show you my real desk.
          </p>
          <p class="margin-note">
            On the code side, you can find me on <a href="https://github.com/Marzogh">GitHub</a>. On the radio side, I
            answer to <strong>VK4MPB</strong>, <strong>VK7MPB</strong>, <strong>VK4ETA</strong>, and
            <strong>VK4GOD</strong>, which still looks like a callsign that ought to summon lightning or require a
            cooldown timer.
          </p>
        </aside>

        <article class="about-story panel">
          <p>
            This site is mixed because I thrive in the sheer variety of the universe. Teaching leaks into ecology,
            ecology leaks into electronics, electronics leak into radio, radio leaks into astrophotography, and all of
            them eventually end up sharing bench space, notebook space, and brain space. Trying to sort all that into
            neat, sealed compartments would be tidier, but it would also be false.
          </p>
          <p>
            A good field survey, a good lesson, a good antenna deployment, and a good imaging session all rely on much
            the same instincts. You look carefully, make a plan, discover the world has edited your plan without
            consulting you, and then adapt with whatever dignity remains. After that, if you are sensible, you write
            down what actually happened so Future You has some chance of being less foolish next time.
          </p>
          <p>
            That is probably the real connective tissue here. I like systems. I like patterns. I like understanding how
            one thing quietly explains another. Sometimes that means cells and ecosystems. Sometimes it means firmware,
            instrumentation, or radio propagation. Sometimes it means painting tiny plastic goblins because patience,
            light, colour, and absurdly fine detail are clearly transferable skills.
          </p>
          <p>
            Everything in this universe is connected, and eventually all of it is heading for entropy soup. In the
            meantime, we can make some temporary, useful, beautiful semblance of order out of the chaos, with full
            knowledge that we are mostly rearranging the chaos while increasing it somewhere else. I do not find that
            bleak. If anything, I find it oddly comforting. It feels like permission to pay attention.
          </p>
          <p>
            So this place ends up being part field notebook, part lab bench, part observatory log, part classroom prep
            book, and part workbench covered in cables, maps, lenses, paint, and whatever else the current problem has
            demanded. If it feels a little unruly, good. The world is unruly. The fun part is trying to understand it
            anyway, and occasionally leaving better notes behind.
          </p>
        </article>
      </section>
    </main>

    <Footer />
  </body>
</html>

<style>
  .about-page {
    max-width: min(1200px, calc(100% - 2 * var(--space-5)));
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--space-6);
  }

  .about-hero {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) minmax(340px, 1fr);
    gap: var(--space-5);
    align-items: center;
    background:
      radial-gradient(820px 260px at top right, rgba(37, 99, 235, 0.10), transparent 72%),
      radial-gradient(620px 220px at bottom left, rgba(34, 197, 94, 0.08), transparent 78%),
      radial-gradient(460px 160px at 60% 10%, rgba(251, 113, 133, 0.08), transparent 76%),
      #fff;
  }

  .about-hero__copy {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--space-4);
  }

  .about-kicker {
    margin: 0;
    font-size: 0.82rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--muted);
  }

  .about-title,
  .about-lede,
  .margin-note,
  .about-story p {
    margin: 0;
  }

  .about-title {
    max-width: 14ch;
  }

  .about-lede {
    max-width: 62ch;
    font-size: 1.08rem;
    color: var(--text-2);
  }

  .about-lede--small {
    font-size: 1rem;
  }

  .about-collage {
    position: relative;
    min-height: 520px;
  }

  .about-shot {
    position: absolute;
    margin: 0;
    padding: 10px;
    border-radius: 24px;
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8);
    box-shadow: var(--shadow-md);
    backdrop-filter: blur(10px);
    overflow: hidden;
  }

  .about-shot :global(img) {
    display: block;
    width: 100%;
    height: 100%;
    object-fit: cover;
    border-radius: 16px;
  }

  .about-shot--portrait {
    top: 0;
    left: 8px;
    width: min(250px, 42%);
    transform: rotate(-3deg);
  }

  .about-shot--radio {
    top: 26px;
    right: 0;
    width: min(430px, 72%);
    transform: rotate(3deg);
  }

  .about-shot--field {
    left: 74px;
    bottom: 0;
    width: min(390px, 66%);
    transform: rotate(-2deg);
  }

  .about-shot--moon {
    right: 28px;
    bottom: 50px;
    width: min(170px, 26%);
    transform: rotate(4deg);
  }

  .about-scribble {
    position: absolute;
    z-index: 3;
    font-size: 0.84rem;
    font-style: italic;
    letter-spacing: 0.02em;
    color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--text-2) 82%, white 18%);
    text-shadow: 0 1px 0 rgba(255,255,255,0.5);
  }

  .about-scribble--one {
    top: 10px;
    right: 54px;
    transform: rotate(-2deg);
  }

  .about-scribble--two {
    left: 20px;
    bottom: 18px;
    transform: rotate(2deg);
  }

  .about-spread {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(280px, 0.8fr) minmax(0, 1.2fr);
    gap: var(--space-5);
    align-items: start;
  }

  .about-margin {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--space-4);
    position: sticky;
    top: 92px;
  }

  .margin-photo {
    margin: 0;
    overflow: hidden;
    border-radius: 18px;
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    box-shadow: var(--shadow-sm);
  }

  .margin-photo :global(img) {
    display: block;
    width: 100%;
    height: auto;
  }

  .margin-note {
    color: var(--text-2);
  }

  .about-story {
    column-count: 2;
    column-gap: var(--space-6);
    background:
      linear-gradient(135deg, rgba(11, 18, 32, 0.03), rgba(37, 99, 235, 0.05)),
      #fff;
  }

  .about-story p {
    break-inside: avoid;
    margin-bottom: 1.2rem;
    color: var(--text-2);
  }

  .about-story p:last-child {
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }

  @media (max-width: 1020px) {
    .about-page {
      max-width: calc(100% - 2 * var(--space-4));
    }

    .about-hero,
    .about-spread {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }

    .about-margin {
      position: static;
    }
  }

  @media (max-width: 720px) {
    .about-collage {
      min-height: 740px;
    }

    .about-shot--portrait {
      left: 0;
      width: min(260px, 70%);
    }

    .about-shot--radio {
      top: 170px;
      right: 0;
      width: min(420px, 88%);
    }

    .about-shot--field {
      left: 8px;
      bottom: 0;
      width: min(390px, 82%);
    }

    .about-shot--moon {
      right: 14px;
      bottom: 214px;
      width: min(170px, 34%);
    }

    .about-scribble--one {
      top: 142px;
      right: 16px;
    }

    .about-story {
      column-count: 1;
    }
  }
</style>
